## Common Git and GitHub Terms

| Term | Simple Meaning |
| --- | --- |
| Repository (repo) | A project tracked by Git |
| Local Repository | A repository stored on your computer |
| Remote Repository | A repository hosted on GitHub or another server |
| Commit | A saved snapshot of changes |
| Branch | A separate line of development |
| `main` | The commonly used name for the primary branch |
| `origin` | The conventional name for the default remote repository |
| `HEAD` | A reference to your current checkout, usually the latest commit on the current branch |
| Staging Area | The area where changes are prepared before committing |
| Merge | Combining changes from different branches |
| Merge Conflict | A situation where Git cannot automatically combine changes |
| Pull Request (PR) | A request to review and merge proposed changes |
| Fork | Your own GitHub copy of someone else's repository |
| Clone | Creating a local copy of a remote repository |
| Fetch | Downloading remote updates without integrating them into your current branch |
| Pull | Fetching and integrating changes from a remote repository |
| Push | Uploading local commits to a remote repository |
| README | A file that explains a project |
| `.gitignore` | A file containing rules for ignoring untracked files |

